            ],
            "source_snippet": "import math\n\ndef find_aiming_point(y1, y2, yw, xb, yb, r):\n    # Check if the ball is already in the goal area\n    if 0 <= yb <= y2:\n        return -1\n    \n    # Calculate the vertical distance from the ball to the wall\n    dy = yw - yb\n    \n    # Calculate the horizontal distance from the ball to the goal\n    dx = 0 - xb\n    \n    # Calculate the angle of incidence\n    theta = math.atan2(dy, dx)\n    \n    # Calculate the distance the ball travels before hitting the wall\n    d1 = math.sqrt(dx**2 + dy**2)\n    \n    # Calculate the distance the ball travels after hitting the wall\n    d2 = math.sqrt((yw - y1)**2 + (0 - xb)**2)\n    \n    # Calculate the total distance the ball travels\n    d_total = d1 + d2\n    \n    # Calculate the angle of reflection\n    phi = math.pi - theta\n    \n    # Calculate the horizontal distance the ball travels after reflection\n    dx_reflected = d2 * math.cos(phi)\n    \n    # Calculate the vertical distance the ball travels after reflection\n    dy_reflected = d2 * math.sin(phi)\n    \n    # Check if the ball hits the goal post after reflection\n    if dy_reflected > y2 - y1:\n        return -1\n    \n    # Calculate the abscissa of the aiming point\n    xw = xb + dx_reflected\n    \n    return xw\n\n# Read input\ninput_line = input().strip()\ny1, y2, yw, xb, yb, r = map(int, input_line.split())\n\n# Find the aiming point\nresult = find_aiming_point(y1, y2, yw, xb, yb, r)\n\n# Print the result\nprint(result)",
